We are moving our test suite from Jest 29 to Jest 30. Here is a typical test file and our npm script. Rewrite them so they work on Jest 30 and list anything else we must check before upgrading.

package.json script: "test:unit": "jest --testPathPattern=unit --maxWorkers"

```js
const mockFs = jest.genMockFromModule('fs');
jest.mock('./Utils.js'); // the file on disk is utils.js
const {load} = require('./loader');

test('loads', () => {
  const spy = jest.fn();
  load(spy);
  expect(spy).toBeCalledWith('a');
  expect(spy).lastCalledWith('b');
  expect(() => load(null)).toThrowError('no callback');
});
```
